# has the English string baked in), so only a single PT-BR dictionary is needed. T() looks the
# English string up in that dictionary when the active language is "PT" and falls back to the
# English text itself whenever the key is missing - so a string that hasn't been translated yet
# just shows up in English instead of breaking.
# ================================================

